From 2256a45d657b06970b20802cab5d8abd15f9916e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ignaciopd3 <210892957+ignaciopd3@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:21:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/24] Casa stays up through the launcher's binding, not as a
 foreground service

TCL's TclAppBoot refuses startForeground to an app started in the background
(bootType start_foreground, reason default_borbid), so CasaService crashed on
start. The launcher now binds it for as long as Home lives; Casa's own parts
talk to it in-process, and the boot receiver and foreground permissions go.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
